+# Vocabulary Audit Performance Hardening
+
+## Outcome
+
+PASS.
+
+The global vocabulary candidate audit was made linear in source-file length and indexed by candidate token relationship. The change preserves the exact governed candidate set while removing repeated full-text newline counting and repeated full-lexicon scans.
+
+## Defect
+
+The prior implementation performed:
+
+- `text.count()` from the beginning of a file for every identifier occurrence; and
+- a full canonical-entry scan for every candidate occurrence.
+
+This created avoidable quadratic behaviour and made the CLI the slowest order-audit node.
+
+## Repair
+
+- Scan identifiers line by line while retaining one-based line and column evidence.
+- Pre-index canonical entries by token count and token-set signature.
+- Restrict nearest-candidate evaluation to relationships capable of reaching the governed score threshold.
+- Add a subprocess timeout to make future non-termination explicit.
+- Add proof for line, column and Python function-declaration context preservation.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Focused audit and canonical-builder proof: `23 passed`.
+- Baseline global candidates: `133`.
+- Repaired global candidates: `133`.
+- Candidate sets: exact match.
+- Resolved occurrence count: `1228` before and after.
+- Report fingerprint changed only because the audited source changed.
+- Single-process active Tier A orders after repair:
+  - forward: `1254 passed`;
+  - reverse: `1254 passed`;
+  - deterministic hash-shuffled: `1254 passed`.
+
+## Files
+
+- `src/nvda_desk/vocabulary_synonym_audit.py`
+- `tests/tier_a/vocabulary/test_vocabulary_synonym_candidate_audit.py`
+- `raw/checkpoint_resume/baseline_global_report.json`
+- `raw/checkpoint_resume/current_global_report.json`
+- `raw/vocabulary_optimisation_final_focused.txt`
